abstract: >-
  OpenLithoHub is a vendor-neutral computational lithography platform:
  full-chip streaming execution (bounded core/halo windows without
  mandatory full-layout raster materialization), artifact-backed and
  self-auditing industrial benchmarking, proof-carrying PASS/FAIL/
  INCONCLUSIVE verification, and deployable CLI / Python / HTTP surfaces.
  It bridges academic tensor-based optimization and industrial mask
  manufacturing through standardized metrics (EPE, PV Band, shot count,
  EUV stochastic robustness),
  MRC/DRC compliance gating, and an end-to-end OASIS workflow that
  supports both Manhattan and curvilinear masks, with a model-agnostic
  evaluation interface for OPC/ILT models.
